      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The main understandability issues are:\n- All test data on one line (line 25) — unreadable\n- Parameter named `expectedDays` but it holds **hours** (misleading)\n- Unused `data_invalid()` method adds noise\n- Unused imports\n\nLet me write the improved test.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made were: formatted the `data_valid()` test data with one entry per line and grouped with explanatory comments, renamed the misleading `expectedDays` parameter to `expectedHours`, removed the unused `data_invalid()` method, and dropped unused imports."
